-- maker.talk: the pattern-size-made-at-run-time case (spec chapter 6,
-- Limits; chapter 8, Compiling). Loaded with patternSize = 50. `unit` is a
-- literal of 30 instructions, so it loads. Splicing it compiles at run time,
-- at `make-pattern`.

script variable unit = <29 digits>
script variable status = "idle"
script variable made = nothing

-- 1 + 29 + 1 = 31 instructions: made.
on small
  put <"x", (unit)> into made
end small

-- 29 + 29 + 1 = 59 instructions: over the limit, a Limit Fault.
on big
  put "started" into status
  put <(unit), (unit)> into made
end big
